  "summary": "Panic on an `EHLO` reply line of only white space allows denial of service",
  "details": "A malicious or compromised server can reply to `EHLO` with a line holding\nnothing but white space, causing the client to panic.\n\nApplications that connect only to a trusted server over implicit TLS are not\nexposed; the risk applies to clients that may connect to untrusted servers, or\nthat use `STARTTLS` or no TLS, where a man-in-the-middle can forge the reply.",
